    > pyenv virtualenv system kgd-env --system-site-packages 
        > System-site-packages is to make pycamera2 happy
            > (https://forums.raspberrypi.com/viewtopic.php?t=361758)
    > git clone https://github.com/ci-group/robohat_ariel && pip install
        > Install useless? Besides dependencies
    > Follow instructions from repo (update/upgrade, install lgpio, ...)
        > Specifically the config part to allow the pins
            > sudo mv /boot/firmware/config.txt /boot/firmware/config.txt.original
            > sudo cp setup_files/config.txt /boot/firmware/config.txt
        > To get a startup sound (copies and rename user/folder)
            > custom randombeep.service to get proper folders/users and tmp folder (should be in my repo)
            > sudo cp apets-ariel/scripts/randombeep.service /lib/systemd/system
            > (check with sudo systemctl daemon-reload; sudo systemctl start randombeep; systemctl status randombeep.service)
        > sudo apt install libcap-dev && pip install picamera 2
        > Make sure to:
            pip uninstall RPi.GPIO
            pip install rpi-lgpio
